# tools/al/ales_stereo_gate_env_witness.rish — stereo_gate_env: the attack/release noise gate carried into stereo, the linked envelope driving one linked gate over time (ALES162).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES162.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-065745_fill-ales162-lotus-stereo-gate-env.md
# Stands on: lotus/stereo_envelope.rye (ALES160 — the linked envelope, its stereo_env_step reused whole), lotus/stereo_gate.rye (ALES156 — the linked gate this drives over time, its memoryless form the unit-coefficient
# limit), lotus/gate_env.rye (ALES54 — the mono attack/release gate, its GateEnvError reused whole and its output the left-always-peak comparison), lotus/gate.rye (ALES51 — the silenced floor),
# lotus/pan.rye (ALES10 — the StereoClip), lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip, sample_max).
#
# lotus/stereo_gate_env.rye gates a span of sample-PAIRS in a master below a magnitude threshold by a ratio, the one downward push following the shared LINKED envelope over time. Each pair advances one shared
# envelope toward the linked peak max(|left|, |right|) by ALES160's step (attack while rising, release while falling): at or above the threshold both pass byte for byte, below it the silenced floor gat = e·den/num
# (ALES51's floor on the linked envelope) yields one gain gat/e applied to both raw samples — one detector, one gate, the image held. GateEnvError (BadThreshold, BadRatio, BadCoeff, BadRange) reused whole; the fusion
# adds no fault. Values only, never a length. The crux is the instantaneous law (unit attack and release reducing it to ALES156's memoryless stereo_gate byte for byte on both — the time-varying rung's zero-smoothing limit
# is exactly the memoryless one already proven), the linked-gate-over-time law (a left-always-peak master with left' equal to ALES54's mono gate_env(left), the right scaled by the same fraction, the independent per-channel
# gate_env differing), the image law (the shared gain preserving the L:R ratio, an out-of-phase pair returning still out of phase), the knob laws (unit ratio the identity, a slower release holding the gate open longer), the
# carry law (a span in two pieces equal to the whole once on both), and the above-threshold/silence/balance/atomicity/degenerate law.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_stereo_gate_env_witness.rish

say "ales-stereo-gate-env: Language EN — stereo_gate_env gates a span of sample-pairs in a stereo master below a magnitude threshold by a ratio, the one downward push following the shared linked envelope over time. Each pair advances one shared envelope toward the linked peak (the max of the two channels' magnitudes, clamped to the rail), the attack fraction while it rises and the release while it falls; where the smoothed envelope sits at or above the threshold the gate is open and both channels pass byte for byte, and where it falls below, the envelope's whole magnitude is divided by the ratio and the single gain (the silenced floor over the envelope) is applied to both raw samples. It validates the threshold, ratio, attack, release, and span once against the shared length before any write, so a refusal never gates one channel and leaves the other torn. It writes values only, never a length, so the two channels leave balanced; the caller owns the envelope across calls, so a span gated in two pieces equals the whole once and the release holds across the boundary."
say "ales-stereo-gate-env: Style Radiant — ALES156's stereo_gate leans on a pair the instant it sees it: a pair below the threshold is quieted the moment it arrives, and the quieting vanishes the moment the pair rises. A real gate breathes — it hears a sound end and holds open through the release before it closes, so the tail of a note is not chopped and the gate does not chatter on every dip between two loud samples. ALES160 built exactly that breath for stereo, one shared envelope tracking the linked peak, and proved it once. This rung spends both proofs: it drives the downward push from the smoothed linked envelope rather than the bare pair, and applies the one resulting gain to both channels — a gate that opens as the sound arrives and stays open patiently as it falls away, the image held to the sample the whole time. Two proofs fused: the detector is linked and time-smoothed (the louder channel deciding the shared loudness over time), and the gate is linked (one silenced gain from the linked envelope applied to both, since gating each channel by its own envelope would open and close on different samples and lurch the image). The crux is six laws: the instantaneous law (unit attack and release making the linked envelope the instantaneous linked peak, so this equals ALES156's memoryless stereo_gate byte for byte on both — the time-varying rung's zero-smoothing limit exactly the memoryless one already proven); the linked-gate-over-time law (a left-always-peak master with the left equal to ALES54's mono gate_env of it byte for byte, the right scaled by the same fraction, the independent per-channel gate_env genuinely differing); the image law (the shared gain preserving the left-to-right ratio, an out-of-phase pair returning still out of phase, no magnitude expanding and no sign flipping); the knob laws (unit ratio the identity everywhere, a slower release holding the gate open longer, monotone); the carry law (a span gated in two pieces equal to gating the whole once, byte for byte on both); and the above-threshold, silence, balance, atomicity, and degenerate law (a master whose linked envelope never falls below the threshold passing byte for byte, silence staying silence, the lengths held, each of the four refusals leaving both channels untouched and balanced, count zero the identity on both)."
say "ales-stereo-gate-env: Lens TAME — two bounded in-process i16 Clips (left, right) carrying one shared i64 envelope, one linked-peak comparison and at most one multiply-then-divide for the envelope step (ALES160's proven stereo_env_step) plus one per channel for the gain, all in i64 (the product of a magnitude and the silenced floor at most 32768 times 32767 never overflowing), the gain gat over e in the closed interval zero to one so every scaled magnitude is at most its input's and fits i16; the two channels enter balanced (the StereoClip invariant asserted on entry) and leave balanced (a gate writes values only, each length asserted equal and within bound on exit, each written sign asserted held); the threshold, ratio, both coefficients, and the span are validated once before either channel is mutated, so a refusal never gates one channel and leaves the other torn; the linked envelope is asserted a legal magnitude in zero to sample_max each sample and the silenced floor within zero to envelope, so the single gain is a genuine reduction; a shared envelope of exactly zero arises only when both channels are silent (asserted), so no divide by zero and nothing to gate; StereoGateEnvError is ALES54's GateEnvError (BadThreshold, BadRatio, BadCoeff, BadRange) reused whole, the fusion adding no fault. The instantaneous law is proven by running both stereo_gate_env under unit attack and release and ALES156's memoryless stereo_gate on the same master and demanding byte-for-byte equality on both channels; the linked-gate-over-time law against a master where the left always holds the peak — the left equal to ALES54's mono gate_env of it byte for byte while the right is scaled by the same fraction, the independent mono gate_env of the right alone shown to genuinely differ; the image law proves no magnitude expands and no sign flips over a mixed master and that an out-of-phase pair returns still exactly out of phase; the knob laws prove unit ratio the identity everywhere and a slower release holding a quiet tail open where an instant release gates it; the carry law proves a span gated in two pieces equal to the whole once on both channels; and the above-threshold, silence, balance, atomicity, and degenerate cases prove an always-loud master passing byte for byte, an all-silent master staying zero, the length held, each of the five refusals leaving both channels untouched and balanced, and an empty span the identity on both; siloed to lotus/, the threshold a magnitude in sample units, the ratio a plain fraction, the attack and release fractions per sample index, no real sample rate, no anti-aliasing, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/stereo_gate_env"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_gate_env.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-stereo-gate-env: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/stereo_gate_env.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-stereo-gate-env: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-stereo-gate-env: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-gate-env' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-gate-env: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-stereo-gate-env line"
